  "title": "Symlink-safe scanning, shared agent skills, and a skills CI gate",
  "summary": "The scan walker in crates/osf/src/scan/mod.rs no longer follows symlinks: collect_files uses symlink_metadata and counts a link as skipped instead of reading through it, and scan_paths re-checks each resolved target so a symlink is counted as excluded rather than reported clean. Five new integration tests cover tracked links, dangling links, explicit symlinked paths, nested links, and cycles. Alongside that, agent configuration is reorganised: repository-internal skills move to .agents/skills/ with .claude/skills as a git symlink to it, folder-scoped AGENTS.md files appear under crates/ and .github/workflows/, and ci.yml gains two steps that lint every shipped skill and assert the .claude/skills symlink mode and target.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
